<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>AphaBatchJobs.Core</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>AphaBatchJobs.Core</AssemblyName>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);1591</NoWarn>
    <!-- Added LangVersion for explicit C# version control and consistency across environments -->
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <!-- Added TreatWarningsAsErrors for production-grade code quality -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <!-- Added deterministic builds for reproducible builds in CI/CD pipelines -->
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <!-- Added continuous integration build flag support -->
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Core abstractions with minimal dependencies -->
    <!-- No external package references needed for domain models, interfaces, and enums -->
    <!-- This layer should remain dependency-free to maintain clean architecture principles -->
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>


<!-- 
Key improvements made following .NET best practices:

1. LangVersion: Explicitly set to 'latest' to ensure consistent C# language features across development environments and build servers

2. Deterministic: Set to 'true' to enable deterministic builds, which is crucial for:
   - Reproducible builds in CI/CD pipelines (AWS CodeBuild, GitHub Actions, etc.)
   - Better debugging experience
   - Compliance and security auditing

3. ContinuousIntegrationBuild: Conditionally enabled when CI environment variable is set, which:
   - Optimizes builds for CI/CD environments
   - Improves source link and debugging information
   - Aligns with AWS CodeBuild and other CI/CD best practices

4. TreatWarningsAsErrors: Explicitly set (currently false) for visibility and easy toggling in production environments

These additions maintain the clean architecture principle (no external dependencies) while improving build reliability, consistency, and alignment with modern .NET and AWS deployment practices.
-->